    <!--
      Hebrew — and the directory name is the load-bearing part.

      ⚠️ THE BUCKET IS `values-iw`, NOT `values-he`. A `values-he` copy compiles,
      ships, reviews as done and renders NOTHING: AAPT2 stores Hebrew under the
      legacy qualifier `iw` and does not fold `he` into it. `Observed:` 2026-08-16
      on a he-IL Samsung — the widget rendered English while its layout mirrored
      correctly to RTL, which is the tell. This file lived in `values-he/` from
      #36 until #51 moved it, so it had never rendered once.
      `HebrewLocaleResourceTest` fails if a `he` bucket comes back.

      ⚠️ AND THE USUAL REASON GIVEN FOR THIS IS WRONG. It is *not* because
      `Locale` reports Hebrew as `iw` — `Observed:` Android 17 / API 37,
      2026-08-16, `Locale.forLanguageTag("he").language` returns `he`, and this
      bucket still resolves (`AppLocaleInstrumentedTest`). Checking that code and
      finding `he` looks like permission to rename this directory. It is not.

      PARTIAL, AND THE TEST SAYS SO. Parity with `values/strings.xml` is
      enforced, so this file is complete with respect to every English string
      that exists — but the `feature/` literal sweep (§7.2) is what *creates*
      those English strings, and it is not finished. See this session's
      CHANGELOG entry for exactly which screens have been swept.

      Wording note (§4.8): a Hebrew prefix attached to a Latin run lays out on
      the far side of it — `ל‑Google Tasks` renders as `Google Tasks‑ל`. These
      strings therefore use standalone words (`אל`, `ואז`) in front of every
      Latin run instead of an attached prefix.

      Terminology (§5.1 / `E1`): the `Goal` entity is יעד, never מטרה.
    -->

